 ## Background
-Greedy Voxel Mesh Optimization is used in voxel engines, particularly those inspired by Minecraft-like games [S1, unofficial]. Mikola Lysenko provided a detailed description of various meshing methods, emphasizing the importance of quad ordering [S2, unofficial]. The specific implementation detailed in the sources, `CEVoxelGreedyOptimizer`, is an unofficial implementation found in a GitHub repository [S1, unofficial].
+Greedy Voxel Mesh Optimization was popularized in the context of voxel engines, particularly those inspired by Minecraft [S2, unofficial]. Mikola Lysenko provided a detailed description of various meshing methods, emphasizing the importance of quad ordering [S2, unofficial]. The specific implementation detailed in the sources, `CEVoxelGreedyOptimizer`, is an unofficial implementation found in a GitHub repository [S1, unofficial]. The technique is widely used in voxel-based games to improve rendering performance by reducing the number of draw calls [S1, unofficial].
 
